    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Kyoto sits in a basin in western Honshu, walled by mountains on three sides. The Kamo River runs north to south through the centre, and the Higashiyama hills rise along its eastern edge.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The city was founded as Heian-kyo in 794 and stayed the imperial capital until 1868. Its streets still follow the original grid. The UNESCO listing for ancient Kyoto covers 17 sites, from Kiyomizu-dera to the gold-leaf Kinkaku-ji. In Gion, geiko and maiko still walk to evening appointments along Hanamikoji.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Late March to early April brings cherry blossom, and mid to late November brings red maples. Both seasons are busy, so reach Fushimi Inari or Arashiyama before 8am.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
